<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why this log exists, who writes it, and what it isn't."
>
  <article class="wrap prose about">
    <p class="eyebrow">whoami</p>
    <h1>Why this log exists</h1>

    <p>
      I run two production sites for the U.S. market — a content site and a
      utility-tools site. Somewhere in the last year, "will Google index this"
      quietly turned into "will an AI even see this," and most of what I found
      written about that shift was either sold by a $1,500-a-month agency or
      written by someone who'd never actually run the fix themselves.
    </p>

    <p>
      So I started keeping a log instead. Every entry here starts from a real
      problem on one of my own sites — a sitemap that silently broke, a batch
      of pages that cannibalized each other, a crawler rule that was quietly
      blocking the thing I wanted indexed — and walks through exactly what I
      did about it, usually with an AI coding agent doing the legwork instead
      of a retainer.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>What you'll find here:</strong> dated write-ups with before/after
      numbers where I have them, the actual prompts and commands I used, and
      honest calls on which parts of the AI-search-optimization playbook seem
      to hold up under testing and which parts don't.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>What you won't find:</strong> a pitch for a retainer, a course,
      or an audit service. If something here saves you the cost of hiring
      someone to do it for you, that's the point.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p class="eyebrow">editorial note</p>
      <p>
        Placeholder copy — swap in your real bio, and decide here whether you
        want to name and link your two live sites directly. Naming them lets
        readers verify every case study against a real, running site, which is
        probably your strongest point of difference — but it's your call to
        make deliberately, not a default I should set for you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Questions, corrections, or a fix you want logged? <a href="mailto:hello@thegeolog.com">hello@thegeolog.com</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

